      "message": "fix(app): import STEP files with empty parameter lists\n\n#887: ruststep 0.4.0 - our pinned STEP parser, newest release - cannot\nparse the empty parameter list `()`, which ISO 10303-21 allows. One dead\n`DRAUGHTING_MODEL('',(),#10);` entity, what HOOPS Exchange exports, made\nthe whole DATA section fail; the reported error pointed at `DATA;`\nbecause entity_list backtracks with many0_ and the outer data_section\nloop discards the failure.\n\nThe fix is merged upstream (ricosjp/ruststep@90fdc935, Feb 2025) but no\nrelease contains it (0.4.0, Sept 2024; release request is upstream #256).\nPin that rev with [patch.crates-io]: upstream still declares 0.4.0, so\ncamcraft-app's `=0.4.0` and truck-stepio's `0.4` both resolve to the\npatched crate unchanged. This is the workspace's one git dependency, a\ndeliberate exception to the crates.io-pin posture; drop the patch when a\nruststep release ships the fix.\n\nFixture empty_list.step is box.step plus the offending entity; verified\nagainst the reported HOOPS file headless: 164 facets with the patch,\nclean syntax error without it.\n\nFixes #887",
